About
================================================================================
TVHData is a data service for the EPG software TV-Browser. It loads the channel
list and the EPG (electronic program guide) from a tvheadend server, so that
TV-Browser shows exactly the channels and programs your tvheadend receives.

TVHData was inspired by VDR DataService by Henrik Niehaus, which does the same
for a VDR (https://github.com/hampelratte/VDR-Data-Service). Many thanks to
Henrik Niehaus. TVHData is a separate project: please ask questions, make
suggestions and report problems at https://github.com/Sagestum/tvhdata.

TVHData works well together with TVHsync (https://github.com/Sagestum/tvhsync),
which manages the recordings of tvheadend from TV-Browser.


Requirements
================================================================================
 * Java 11 or newer
 * TV-Browser >= 4.2.3
 * tvheadend 4.2 or newer with the HTTP API enabled (default)


Installation
================================================================================
 1. Copy TVHData.jar into the plugin directory of TV-Browser
    (e.g. ~/.var/app/org.tvbrowser.TVBrowser/.config/tvbrowser/4.2.7/plugins
    for the flatpak) and restart TV-Browser.
 2. Settings -> Plugins/Data services -> TVHData: enter the URL of tvheadend
    (e.g. http://192.168.1.11:9981), user name and password if needed, and
    optionally choose a channel tag to limit the channel list.
 3. Settings -> Channels: refresh the channel list and add the channels of the
    group "tvheadend".
 4. Update the TV data as usual.

tvheadend only knows the EPG from now on. Programs of today, which have already
been shown, are kept from the previous update.


